eople might  not realize what goes on behind the  scenes  i'm curious what do you think actually  would surprise people to learn  about being like a live streamer being a  professional gamer  i have spent probably eight times more  like you know in terms of total time  editing than i ever have filming or  playing games in the last six and a half  years  like i think people don't think you just  like oh it's a 10 minute video dude he  plays games for 10 minutes  adds a couple cuts or sends it off to  another it's like i edit my own videos  like  i come up with my own ideas i do my own  filming like i do the whole process  and you know those times where i was  doing like you know five or six videos a  week  when i was in my real big growth stage  and i was sleeping three or four hours a  night sometimes  like you know like i'm lucky i had such  a loving mother that could put up with  my crap and i was still living at my  parents house  and she'd like cook for me and clean up  after me and stuff and i was so lucky to  have that  because i was a zombie i was a zombie  doing that so i think that's my biggest  thing is like people think it's easy  and obviously you know we are very lucky  to do it because we're passionate about  what we do every day you know there can  be a lot of money in and stuff  but that doesn't mean it's easy if that  makes sense like i was a construction  worker before this  and that was definitely a lot easier so  yeah you know something i have a buddy  who does construction and i try  explaining to people i'm like  to me that is uh like i i don't want to  say a real job  but like if you're standing in the sun  like doing what you got i mean that's a  completely different beast  yeah yeah like so i think there's just  different challenges in every career  path i think  and i don't blame people for thinking  those things i thought the same thing  before i got into it  um it's just yeah it does surprise you  how much actual work  goes into everything and to getting  everything right especially once you get  to a bigger and bigger scale  one of the things that i love about  video games is every year it seems like  the technology gets better and better  the games get more immersive what do you  think games are on like the cusp of  being able to do  that they currently can't do what are  you looking forward to i'm looking  forward to when  we can have a full vr experience which  in a lot of ways you kind of already can  like even those games like it's kind of  happening in the background  but i have a friend who has made a lot  of vr videos so i used to sort of see  what he  would do and just the way you can  interact in those worlds now  and you know the future of like you know  all of that  and maybe that's still 20 years away for  it to be properly perfect but i think  that's just going to change  every immersion immersive experience  that we have  um in terms of how we see movies and how  we see entertainment productions  how we see games all of that i think  it's all going to change like with  virtual reality  i i completely completely agree  what's a game that you wish more people  knew about  i've i've been asked this a couple of  times i wish i had an  answer just because i have slacked so  much in like the indie scene in the last  couple years focusing mostly just on the  big projects of like the big games  um like i i don't know that's a tough  one like i've been  i think on the big scale i think games  have been slacking a lot lately there  hasn't really been that big game that  sort of  you know captured people lately and i  definitely haven't had my finger on the  indie scene so i don't know if i  necessarily have an answer for that  um i still play runescape every now and  then  old school runescape so if you know more  people could play that that'd be nice  well that that's another thing it's like  you obviously do you get to play  games like do you want to play games for  fun at this point is it  